Approach: Two Pointer (Greedy)
Take two pointers:
i = 0 (start)
j = n - 1 (end)
Calculate area:
Width = j - i
Height = min(height[i], height[j])
Area = width × height
Move the pointer which has smaller height, because:
Area depends on minimum height
If we move the larger height pointer → area will always decrease
So we move the smaller height pointer to try getting a larger height
Keep updating max area.

Time Complexity: O(n)
Space Complexity: O(1)
